Let a profession tool banked in the reagent vault satisfy a recipe.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp

Why: bug report #29 -- "Bought a blacksmith hammer, didn't go into inventory
or into reagent bank, need it for crafting."

Tools are reagent-vault material by IsReagentItem (IsToolItem covers
ITEM_CLASS_WEAPON / ITEM_SUBCLASS_WEAPON_MISC -- Mining Pick, Skinning
Knife, Blacksmith Hammer, Arclight Spanner), so one is pulled out of the bag
the moment it is acquired. That half worked. What did not work is that a
banked tool cannot satisfy the recipe that needs it:

  Reagent[]        materials      TopUpReagentFromVault covers this
  Totem[]          a named item   nothing covered this
  TotemCategory[]  a tool kind    nothing covered this

Totem[] and TotemCategory[] are checked further down CheckItems with
HasItemCount / HasItemTotemCategory, both of which walk real inventory only.
So the hammer was banked, visible in the reagent panel, and useless -- every
blacksmithing recipe still said you needed a hammer. Core-patch 0020
explicitly left totem requirements alone; this is the follow-up that covers
them, and it covers them by SUPPLYING the tool rather than by waiving the
check, which is the right shape for a requirement that is real.

Unlike a reagent, a tool is not consumed, so TopUpToolFromVault hands it back
permanently instead of topping up per cast. After the first craft the player
is simply holding their hammer again.

Paired with a module-side change in DefaultLootAction: only the FIRST copy of
a tool is banked, and later copies stay in the bag. The bot accounts had
accumulated 30-75 Blacksmith Hammers apiece, which is a tool sink, not a
convenience.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ near the other Living Gear forward declarations
+void LivingGear_TopUpToolFromVault(Player* player, uint32 totemCategory);

@@ Spell::CheckItems, immediately before the Totem / TotemCategory checks
+        for (int i = 0; i < 2; ++i)
+        {
+            if (m_spellInfo->Totem[i] != 0 && !player->HasItemCount(m_spellInfo->Totem[i]))
+                LivingGear_TopUpReagentFromVault(player, m_spellInfo->Totem[i], 1);
+            if (m_spellInfo->TotemCategory[i] != 0)
+                LivingGear_TopUpToolFromVault(player, m_spellInfo->TotemCategory[i]);
+        }
+
         // check totem-item requirements (items presence in inventory)
         uint32 totems = 2;
